---
// Neutral editorial framing for the homepage. The goal is to look like a
// trustworthy comparison directory, not a self-serving ranked advertorial.
---

<section class="mb-12 space-y-10 not-prose">
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800">
    <p class="text-base leading-7 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      MediaPlanningTool.com tracks media planning tools by use case: lightweight planning, agency workflow,
      enterprise planning and buying, audience research, TV reach and frequency, and reporting. The goal is to
      help planners compare tradeoffs quickly — pricing transparency, data depth, channel coverage, workflow fit,
      and whether a platform is built for planning only or planning plus buying.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="mb-5 flex items-end justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Start by use case</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          There is no universal “best” media planning tool. The right shortlist depends on the planning job.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <a href="/halliard" class="block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 transition hover:border-primary-300 hover:shadow-md dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400">Free / lightweight</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Individual planners</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Good fit when you need quick omnichannel planning, calculators, or a lightweight starting point before enterprise procurement.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/basis" class="block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 transition hover:border-primary-300 hover:shadow-md dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400">Enterprise suites</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Agency planning + buying</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Best evaluated when workflow, buying integrations, approvals, reporting, and cross-team operations matter as much as planning math.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/nielsen-media-impact" class="block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 transition hover:border-primary-300 hover:shadow-md dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400">TV / cross-media</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Reach and frequency</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Relevant for planners who need established audience data, TV/CTV scenario planning, and cross-media measurement context.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/bionic" class="block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 transition hover:border-primary-300 hover:shadow-md dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-600 dark:text-primary-400">Workflow</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Flowcharts and budgets</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Useful when the bottleneck is organizing plans, maintaining versions, building flowcharts, and keeping budget details consistent.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6 dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800/60">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">How we compare tools</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Use-case fit</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Who the tool is actually built for.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Pricing clarity</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Published pricing, free tiers, or procurement complexity.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Planning depth</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">R&F, scenarios, audience data, and budget allocation.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Workflow</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Approvals, exports, collaboration, and flowcharts.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Tradeoffs</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Where a tool is strong, weak, overkill, or too narrow.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5 dark:border-amber-900/60 dark:bg-amber-950/20">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-50">Independence disclosure</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
      Halliard is listed in this directory because it is a media planning tool. That relationship is disclosed here so readers can judge the comparison fairly. Placements are not sold, and the directory should remain useful even when Halliard is not the right fit.
    </p>
  </section>
</section>
